From 28355eb3c9a47e27c684370a618e7b2a53128b1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:41:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 32/35] nx2: passthrough backend: macro parameters by
 reference, barrier releases promised, late hardware acquires

- EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_BYREF=1: an entry that is the rest of a 3D macro call (MKW's GPU-culled parameters) is
  submitted as a GP entry on the guest's own words (SYNC_WAIT), announced by a header, in one submission
  with the call, instead of a drain of every channel and a CPU copy.
- Barrier QMDs launched from memory promise their releases: guest memory with the stream's small inline
  uploads laid over it (Eglantine writes NVN's payload patches on its back thread, later).
- EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_HWACQ_LATE=1 (experimental): an acquire the front waits at becomes a host acquire once
  the submitted work meets it.
- Stats lines split (the logger cuts long lines); the last kept acquires are logged when the backend stops.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
